<title>USA: Dresser elects top executives.</title>
<headline>Dresser elects top executives.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dresser Industries Inc said on Friday that it has elected president and chief executive officer William Bradford chairman and chief executive.</p>
<p>Executive vice president Donald Vaughn will become president and chief operating officer, Textron said.</p>
<p>The changes become effective December 1, 1996, when chairman John Murphy and vice chairman Bill St. John retire, the company said.</p>
<p>George Juetten was named chief financial officer effective, December 1, 1996, Dresser said.  </p>
<p>Bill St. John, the current vice chairman, serves as chief financial officer, a Dresser Industries spokesman said.</p>
</text>
